# Session continuity (always on)

Durable context lives in git-tracked markdown. Chat history is not the source of truth.

## Required at session start

1. Read `PROJECT_STATUS.md` (aim, current focus, done, next).
2. Read `ENGINEERING_STANDARDS.md` (language, chat style, coding rules per service).
3. Follow the `session-continuity` and `engineering-standards` skills.
4. Briefly acknowledge aim + current focus (1–2 short sentences) when starting work in a new chat.

## Required during / after work

- After meaningful progress, task switches, or wrap-up: update `PROJECT_STATUS.md`.
- All generated code must follow `ENGINEERING_STANDARDS.md`.
- Never store secrets or API keys in status or standards files.
- Remind the user to commit and push these markdown files so the next session inherits them; do not commit unless asked.
